{"article_id": "6c9b16c709557adb", "body_text": "", "club": "Manchester United", "club_candidates": ["Manchester United"], "crawl_method": "rss", "event_date": "", "extraction_confidence": 0.5, "journalist": "Jacob Steinberg", "language": "English", "normalized_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/may/19/manchester-united-liverpool-chelsea-target-jarrod-bowen-west-ham-transfer", "player": "", "player_candidates": [], "provider": "guardian_rss", "published_at": "Tue, 19 May 2026 15:25:48 GMT", "seen_at": "2026-05-21T03:48:09.315206+00:00", "snippet": "<ul><li><p>West Ham will need to raise more than £100m if relegated</p></li><li><p>Relegation could force England player to reassess future</p></li></ul><p>Chelsea, Liverpool and Manchester United are interested in Jarrod Bowen as rival clubs prepare to capitalise on West Ham’s financial problems by targeting their best players.</p><p>West Ham will need to raise more than £100m if relegated from the Premier League and there is growing interest in Bowen from a host of top sides.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/may/19/manchester-united-liverpool-chelsea-target-jarrod-bowen-west-ham-transfer\">Continue reading...</a>", "source": "The Guardian Football RSS", "title": "Manchester United, Liverpool and Chelsea target Jarrod Bowen amid drop threat", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/football/2026/may/19/manchester-united-liverpool-chelsea-target-jarrod-bowen-west-ham-transfer"}
